  "body": "Asked for by Mike (collaborator) on 2026-11-18, after a Windows 11 user's \"it kept crashing\" report: \"We should add some/most of that in a FAQ or Windows Troubleshooting on CamCraft docs for Windows users.\"\n\nA new page in the user guide (site/content/guide/, linked from the install page and the FAQ), plain language:\n\n1. **The app does not start or closes at once:** start it with another graphics backend - a shortcut with `--gpu-backend dx12`, `vulkan` or `gl` added to Target. What each means, in one line each.\n2. **The whole PC freezes, the screen shows \"snow\"** (seen on a desktop Ryzen 5 with onboard Radeon): this is a graphics driver or hardware hang that CamCraft's 3D view triggers, not a CamCraft crash. Checks, in order: the latest AMD/Intel/NVIDIA driver from the vendor's site; onboard graphics use main RAM, so try the BIOS RAM profile (XMP/EXPO) off and set \"UMA Frame Buffer Size\" to 2-4 GB; BIOS update; temperatures.\n3. **Testing the PC itself:** free tools by name and what each tests - MemTest86 (RAM, from USB), OCCT (CPU/RAM/graphics with temperatures), HWiNFO64 (temperatures). Note: save work first.\n4. **What to send us:** `dxdiag` -> \"Save All Information\" (note it contains the PC name), the CamCraft log file and where it is (once #2421 lands), the version, and the step where it failed. Where to send it (GitHub issue or Discord).\n5. **Windows on ARM / virtual machines:** the x64 build runs under emulation; it worked on a Parallels ARM VM using the software renderer, slower.\n\nDone means: the page exists in the guide, is linked from the install page, and builds with `zola build`. No claims we have not tested; tools are named, not endorsed.\n",
